                <head>293. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On November 5, 1965, President Johnson
                    signed two bills releasing minerals held in U.S. stockpiles. H.R. 9047
                    authorized the release of 200,000 tons of zinc; H.R. 10305, 200 million pounds
                    of nickel. For text of his statement, see <hi rendition="#italic">Public Papers
                        of the Presidents of the United States: Lyndon
                            B. Johnson, 1965</hi>, Book II, pages 1098–1099.</p>
            </div>
